RDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-09-10T13:00:00Z by TEAM_LEAD (project): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\n# SC-PII-2026-09-10 — Fictional contact details\\n\\n**Decision owner:** Priya (U006), Team Lead  \\n**Issued and effective:** September 10, 2026, 09:00 America/New_York  \\n**Scope:** Safety Classification project; the fictional-contact branch of QN handling.\\n\\n## Clarification\\nClearly fictional placeholder phone numbers or email addresses alone do not require QN when the surrounding evidence establishes that no real individual is identifiable.\\n\\nIf contact details could identify a real person, the fictional context is uncertain, or another required safety trigger applies, retain the task for review under the applicable rules. This clarification does not waive those separate controls.\\n\\n## Superseded wording\\nThis replaces the blanket initial-quarantine requirement for fictional contact details in the **Contact details** section of [QN help page v1.0](../../instructions/history/safety_qn_help_page_v1.0.md). It does not invalidate unrelated controls in that page.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0\", \"title\": \"Scoped fictional-PII clarification posted\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1789135200.700004\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1789135200.700004\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"channel_announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-11T14:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-11T14:00:00Z\